d near urban regions or recent burn scars. Notable\n\nevents included flash flooding in the Texas Hill Country, Ruidoso\n\n(New Mexico), New York City (New York), Chicago (Illinois), and\n\nMilwaukee (Wisconsin) among others. In many instances, low\n\nNational Flood Insurance Program (NFIP) take up rates meant\n\nmost of the flood-related damage went uninsured.\n\nInsured Loss (USD bn; Today's Dollars)\n\n700-\n\n600-\n\n500-\n\n400-\n\n300-\n\n200-\n\n100-\n\n648\n\nーーニニ\n\n2000\n\n• United States\n\n2002\n\n2004\n\n• Rest of World\n\n2006\n\n2008\n\n2010\n\nPrevious year va\n\n2012\n\n2014\n\n1 2025 USD using US CPI.\n\n2016\n\n2018\n\n2020\n\n2022\n\n2024\n\nSeptember 2025.\n\nFigure 14: SCS insured losses from 2000 to 2025 YTD; US compared to the rest of the world Loss Data & Graphic: Gallagher Re\n\n23", "width": 1654, "height": 2339, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Major Event Reviews", "bbox": {"x": 638.2, "y": 2086.9, "width": 914.2, "height": 92.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "US & Europe: Severe Convective Storm", "bbox": {"x": 818.5, "y": 1961.6, "width": 733.5999999999999, "height": 40.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "JS SCS YTD: Economic", "bbox": {"x": 1300.5, "y": 1869.6, "width": 251.9000000000001, "height": 28.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "losses reached USD61 billion", "bbox": {"x": 1246.4, "y": 1835.8, "width": 309.0999999999999, "height": 23.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "as the portion covered by", "bbox": {"x": 1277.0, "y": 1795.0, "width": 278.5, "height": 27.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "insurance is now up to", "bbox": {"x": 1311.0, "y": 1761.0, "width": 244.5, "height": 23.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "JSD46 billion", "bbox": {"x": 1399.3, "y": 1727.1, "width": 152.79999999999995, "height": 27.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "US: Insured SCS losses", "bbox": {"x": 943.9, "y": 1869.6, "width": 245.10000000000002, "height": 26.700000000000045}}, {"kind": "t